{
  "_about": "GSTR-2A canonical layer - which raw sheet feeds which canonical table and how each field is located (spec: docs/GSTR2A_CANONICAL_SPEC.md). Every 2A sheet has a title, a 1-3 row wrapped heading block (group headings such as 'Invoice details' above sub-headings), a period banner row ('Financial Year | Tax Period') per month and that month's rows under it; the amendment sheets (B2BA, CDNRA) repeat a sub-heading row right after every banner. The original reader took every column by FIXED POSITION ('pos' below, unchanged). The converter now also READS THE HEADINGS: 'match' = alternatives (each a list of fragments that must all appear, compared after lower-casing and stripping non-alphanumerics, in that column's combined heading text; a group heading directly above the heading row that spans several columns is applied to the columns it spans); 'none' = fragments that must NOT appear. A field is taken from its 'pos' if the heading there matches; if not, from the one other unused column whose heading matches (warning W703); if none, from 'pos' anyway as the original did (warning W704). 'type': 'num' = converted to a number (blank = 0), 'raw' = kept exactly as in the source. 'required': true = the sheet is unusable (error E701) if the field cannot be located at all. 'gstin_field' = the column whose value must be GSTIN-shaped for a row to be genuine data; 'doc_field' = the document-number column whose '-Total' rollup row is kept (null = no rollup logic, as for ISD).",
  "version": "1",
